{"name":"Ruggero Grey","hex":"#484435","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ruggero","blocks":[{"text":"Ruggero, the Italian equivalent of Roger, may refer to:"},{"items":["Ruggero I of Sicily (1031–1101) Norman king of Sicily","Ruggero J. Aldisert (1919–2014), judge on the United States Court of Appeals for the Third Circuit","Ruggero Berlam (1854–1920), Italian architect","Ruggero Bonghi (1826–1895), Italian scholar, writer and politician","Ruggero Borghi, former Italian professional road bicycle racer","Ruggero Cobelli (1838–1921), Italian entomologist","Ruggero Deodato, controversial Italian film director, actor and screenwriter, best known for directing horror films","Ruggero Ferrario (1897–1976), Italian racing cyclist and Olympic champion in track cycling","Ruggero Leoncavallo (1857–1919), Italian opera composer","Ruggero Luigi Emidio Antici Mattei (1811–1883), Italian prelate of the Roman Catholic Church","Ruggero Maccari (1919–1989), Italian screenwriter","Ruggero Maregatti (1905–1963), Italian athlete who competed mainly in the 100 metres","Ruggero Marzoli, Italian professional road bicycle racer","Ruggero Mastroianni (1929–1996), Italian film editor","Ruggero Oddi (1864–1913), Italian physiologist and anatomist","Pier Ruggero Piccio (1880–1965), Italian aviator and the founding Chief of Staff of the Italian Air Force","Ruggero Raimondi, Italian Bass-Baritone opera singer and sometime screen actor","Ruggero Santilli, Italian-American physicist and a proponent of fringe theories","Ruggero Verity, Italian entomologist who specialised in butterflies"]}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Ruggero_Guarini.jpg/330px-Ruggero_Guarini.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruggero","wikidata":"Q10862457"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Grey_Longhaired_Female_Cat.jpg/330px-Grey_Longhaired_Female_Cat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Grey_Longhaired_Female_Cat.jpg/330px-Grey_Longhaired_Female_Cat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrey_Longhaired_Female_Cat.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Whistlers_Mother_high_res.jpg/500px-Whistlers_Mother_high_res.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Whistlers_Mother_high_res.jpg/1280px-Whistlers_Mother_high_res.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Whistlers_Mother_high_res.jpg/500px-Whistlers_Mother_high_res.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWhistlers_Mother_high_res.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/FullMoon2010.jpg/500px-FullMoon